  "cv_sections": {
    "preamble": "Amine Bouchmel.pdf | Coordonnées\nwww.linkedin.com/in/amine-\nbouchmel  (LinkedIn)\nPrincipales compétences\nArtificial Intelligence (AI)\nSAS IFRS9\nGroovy",
    "certs": "SAS Certified Specialist: Base\nProgramming Using SAS 9.4\nProgramming for SAS Viya\nNeural Networks and Deep Learning\nMicrosoft Certified: Azure Data\nFundamentalsAmine Bouchmel\nSenior Data & AI Consultant\nTunis, Gouvernorat Tunis, Tunisie\nRésumé\nI’m a Senior Data & AI Consultant with experience delivering\nadvanced analytics, automation, and AI solutions across the\nbanking, energy, and technology sectors. I’ve implemented SAS\nIFRS9, SAS Viya, and Visual Analytics platforms, and developed\nGen AI powered web applications using Python, React, and GPT\nAPIs integrating LLM workflows, prompt engineering, and data\nreasoning to enable natural language analysis and automated\nreporting.\nOutside of my consulting work, I’m deeply involved in independent\nresearch on Large Language Models (LLMs) studying their core\narchitecture, training dynamics, and transformer internals, and\nbuilding proofs of concept to explore how these systems can reason,\nadapt, and interact with structured data.\nMy current focus lies at the intersection of LLM interpretability,\nhybrid AI architectures, and domain-specific GenAI applications.\nI’m particularly interested in how transformer-based models can\nbe optimized, specialized, and safely integrated into enterprise\nworkflows.\nExpérience\nEY\n3 ans 5 mois\nSenior Data & AI Consultant\noctobre 2024 - Present  (1 an 5 mois)\nTunis, Tunisia\nData & AI Consultant\noctobre 2022 - septembre 2024  (2 ans)\nTunis, Tunisia\nSentinel Data\nData Scientist\n  Page 1 of 2\n   \nmars 2022 - août 2022  (6 mois)\nTunis, Tunisia\nFormation\nÉstiam • École supérieure des technologies de l'information\nappliquées aux métiers\nMaster's degree, Big Data & Artificial Intelligence  · (octobre 2023 - juin 2024)\nEsgitech\nMaster's degree, Data Science  · (octobre 2022 - juin 2024)\nFaculté des Sciences Mathématiques, Physiques et Naturelles de\nTunis\nLicence, Ingénierie logicielle  · (septembre 2019 - juin 2022)\n  Page 2 of 2 | Data Science |  |"
  },
